{
  "name": "Records Store (HTTP)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Keep website records on your own server\n\nOne small store that other workflows call to keep, read and drop rows. This one talks to a records API on a server you run.\n\n### How it works\n**Three operations, one contract.** `keep` adds a row, or writes its fields over the row whose `key` field has the same value. `read` returns one item per row, each with the time it was kept as `at`. `drop` removes rows added before a time; a row with a key has no age and stays.\n\nA caller never knows where rows live. Point its **Execute Workflow** node at this workflow or at the Google Sheets store: both take the same inputs and return the same items.\n\nEach request is tried five times, five seconds apart, so a short outage of the server costs nothing.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Create a **Header Auth** credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer <your token>`. Bind it on the four request nodes.\n2. In **Set Store Config**, set `records_url` to the API's address without a trailing slash.\n3. Activate, then select this workflow in each caller's store node.\n\nThe API: `POST {url}/{table}` with `{ row, key }`, `GET {url}/{table}?since=`, `DELETE {url}/{table}?before=`.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "b8d2f3e1-18a1-4c00-9a01-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send one operation to the API\n\nThe caller picks keep, read or drop. Rows come back flat, one item each.",
